 "headline": "In the worst 10% of S&P 500 weeks since 1962 (194 high-inflation and 145 low-inflation tail weeks), 10y Treasuries returned -0.17% a week when real-time CPI inflation exceeded 3% versus +0.33% otherwise; the high-minus-low gap is -0.50 points (block-bootstrap 95% CI [-0.85, -0.20]), so the pre-specified claim is YES, but the gap is -0.28 pp (CI [-0.64, +0.13]) within 1962-1999 and -0.25 pp (CI [-0.77, +0.37]) within 2000-2026, and the breakeven tests are inconclusive."
